===Tunisia vs England===
The two teams had met in two matches, including one game at the [[1998 FIFA World Cup]] group stage, an England [[1998 FIFA World Cup Group G#England vs Tunisia|2–0]] victory.<ref name=Kit15>{{cite web|url=https://resources.fifa.com/image/upload/2018-fifa-world-cup-russiatm-statistical-kit.pdf?cloudid=fjqkfby8aur1lxnvnxdi|title=2018 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit|publisher=FIFA|page=15|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180513163755/http://resources.fifa.com/image/upload/2018-fifa-world-cup-russiatm-statistical-kit.pdf?cloudid=fjqkfby8aur1lxnvnxdi|archive-date=13 May 2018|df=dmy-all}}</ref>

England scored in the 11th minute when [[Mouez Hassen]] stopped a [[John Stones]]' header from a corner from the left, but could not save a [[Harry Kane]] follow-up from close range. Hassen was substituted four minutes later for [[Farouk Ben Mustapha]] due to an injury earlier in the game, after he had a collision with [[Jesse Lingard]]. Lingard then mishit a volley from [[Ashley Young]]'s cross to the far post.<ref name="Goal Tunisia v England">{{cite web |last=McGee |first=Nicholas |title=Captain Kane saves Three Lions |url=http://www.goal.com/en-us/match/tunisia-v-england/report/4k8fq1mudpghgl8eax1zpyax |website=Goal.com |date=18 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180625144300/http://www.goal.com/en-us/match/tunisia-v-england/report/4k8fq1mudpghgl8eax1zpyax |archive-date=25 June 2018 |df=dmy-all }}</ref> After 10 minutes, [[Ferjani Sassi]] equalised from the penalty spot after [[Kyle Walker]] was penalised for an elbow on [[Fakhreddine Ben Youssef]].<ref name="BBC Tunisia v England">{{cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil |title=Tunisia 1 England 2 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44434276 |work=BBC Sport |date=18 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180619045717/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44434276 |archive-date=19 June 2018 |df=dmy-all }}</ref> Kane had an appeal for a penalty waved away within five minutes of the restart as he was seemingly impeded by a pair of Tunisia players at a corner.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2018/jun/18/tunisia-england-world-cup-match-report|title=Kane double ensures England defeat Tunisia in World Cup opener|date=19 June 2018|work=Guardian|access-date=19 June 2018|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180618223854/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2018/jun/18/tunisia-england-world-cup-match-report|archive-date=18 June 2018|df=dmy-all}}</ref> In the additional time, [[Harry Maguire]] flicked a [[Kieran Trippier]] corner from the right into the path of Kane, who headed it inside the goal after being left free at the back post.<ref name="Goal Tunisia v England"/><ref name="TUN-ENG recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/england-harry-kane-tunisia-world-cup |title=England kick off campaign with hard-fought victory |publisher=FIFA |date=18 June 2018 |access-date=18 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520044636/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/england-harry-kane-tunisia-world-cup |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref>

England scored more than once for the first time in 10 World Cup matches, since a [[2006 FIFA World Cup Group B#Sweden vs England|2–2]] draw against Sweden in 2006. Kane became the first England player to score a brace in a World Cup match since [[Gary Lineker]] against Cameroon in [[1990 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Cameroon vs England|1990]].<ref name="BBC Tunisia v England"/>

