===Belgium vs Tunisia===
The two teams had faced each other in three matches, including one game at the [[2002 FIFA World Cup]] group stage, which ended in a [[2002 FIFA World Cup Group H#Tunisia vs Belgium|1–1]] draw.<ref name=Kit15/>

Just 6 minutes into the game, [[Syam Ben Youssef]]'s late challenge on [[Eden Hazard]] was deemed, with the use of VAR, to have been just inside the area and he stepped up to score the penalty into the bottom-left corner. Ten minutes later, [[Dries Mertens]] won possession just inside the Tunisia half before driving forward and passing the ball to [[Romelu Lukaku]]. Lukaku then shot a low strike across [[Farouk Ben Mustapha]] into the bottom-right corner. [[Wahbi Khazri]]'s free-kick from the left was met by [[Dylan Bronn]], who flashed a header past [[Thibaut Courtois]]. [[Thomas Meunier]] found Lukaku inside the area, which he clipped over the onrushing Mustapha. [[Toby Alderweireld]]'s long pass from defence was taken on the chest by Hazard, who then rounded Mustapha to stroke into an empty net. [[Michy Batshuayi]] met [[Youri Tielemans]]' cross at the back post with a controlled half-volley to score Belgium's 5th. Khazri scored deep into stoppage time after a swivel in the box.<ref>{{cite web |last=Atkinson |first=Guy |title=Lukaku and Hazard shine as Red Devils run riot |url=http://www.goal.com/en-in/match/belgium-v-tunisia/xla9emo05rkwo9bx4bxnr8x5 |website=Goal.com |date=23 June 2018}}</ref><ref name="BEL-TUN recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/belgium-dazzle-in-seven-goal-thriller |title=Belgium dazzle in seven-goal thriller |publisher=FIFA |date=23 June 2018 |access-date=23 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520050218/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/belgium-dazzle-in-seven-goal-thriller |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref>

Lukaku became the first player since [[Diego Maradona]] to score back-to-back braces in consecutive world cup games.<ref>{{cite web|title=Belgium's Romelu Lukaku first to score back-to-back World Cup braces since Maradona|url=http://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/story/3540368/belgiums-romelu-lukaku-first-to-score-back-to-back-world-cup-braces-since-maradona|date=23 June 2018|access-date=23 June 2018|publisher=[[ESPN FC]]|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180624054650/http://www.espn.com/soccer/fifa-world-cup/story/3540368/belgiums-romelu-lukaku-first-to-score-back-to-back-world-cup-braces-since-maradona|archive-date=24 June 2018|df=dmy-all}}</ref> Hazard's penalty was Belgium's second quickest goal in a World Cup match (5:59), behind only [[Léopold Anoul]]'s goal [[1954 FIFA World Cup Group 4#England vs Belgium|against England in 1954]], in the fifth minute.<ref>{{cite web |last=Bevan |first=Chris |title=Belgium 5 Tunisia 2 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439152 |work=BBC Sport |date=23 June 2018}}</ref> For Tunisia, it has registered as their worst defeat ever in their World Cup history.

