===England vs Panama===
The two teams had never met before.<ref name=Kit/>

[[John Stones]] headed in from [[Kieran Trippier]]'s corner to open the scoring. [[Harry Kane]] converted a penalty to make it 2–0 following a foul on [[Jesse Lingard]], who was next to find the net with a curling finish with his right foot from the edge of the area. Stones nodded home the rebound after goalkeeper [[Jaime Penedo]] had kept out [[Raheem Sterling]]'s close-range header. Kane scored his second penalty of the match in the stoppage time of first half, hammering the ball into Penedo's top right corner after referee had spotted a foul on the forward by [[Fidel Escobar]]. Kane completed his [[List of FIFA World Cup hat-tricks|hat-trick]] with a deflection near the edge of the box off a shot from [[Ruben Loftus-Cheek]]. [[Felipe Baloy]] scored Panama's first-ever World Cup goal, with a half-volley from a [[Ricardo Ávila]] free-kick.<ref>{{cite web |last=Lancaster |first=Rob |title=Kane hat-trick sees Southgate's side sail through |url=http://www.goal.com/en-in/match/england-v-panama/report/1nxy9zcrz72hqrklyzi0arfft |website=Goal.com |date=24 June 2018}}</ref> The result ensured that both England and Belgium would advance to the knockout stage, while Tunisia and Panama would be eliminated at the group stage.

[[Gary Lineker]] was the last England player before Kane to notch more than one goal in consecutive World Cup matches, 32 years ago. At Mexico 1986, Lineker followed up a hat-trick against Poland with a brace against Paraguay.<ref name="ENG-PAN recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/england-romp-past-panama-and-into-last-16-2967323 |title=England romp past Panama and into last 16 |publisher=FIFA |date=24 June 2018 |access-date=24 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520050750/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/england-romp-past-panama-and-into-last-16-2967323 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref> This was England's biggest win at a major tournament. Stones became the first England defender to score two goals in a World Cup match. Kane is the first player to score at least twice in both of his first two World Cup appearances since [[Grzegorz Lato]] of Poland in 1974.<ref>{{cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil |title=England 6 Panama 1 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439183 |work=BBC Sport |date=24 June 2018}}</ref> Kane is the third England player to score a hat-trick in a World Cup match, after [[Geoff Hurst]] against Germany in the [[1966 FIFA World Cup Final|1966 final]] and Gary Lineker [[1986 FIFA World Cup Group F#England vs Poland|against Poland in 1986]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Law |first=Matt |title=England hat-trick hero Harry Kane 'irreplaceable' at World Cup, says manager Gareth Southgate |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-cup/2018/06/24/england-hat-trick-hero-harry-kane-irreplaceable-world-cup-says/ |publisher=The Telegraph |date=24 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180624182336/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-cup/2018/06/24/england-hat-trick-hero-harry-kane-irreplaceable-world-cup-says/ |archive-date=24 June 2018 |df=dmy-all }}</ref>

