===England vs Belgium===
The two teams had met in 21 matches, including two matches at the World Cup, one round of 16 game at the [[1990 FIFA World Cup]] which ended in a [[1990 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#England vs Belgium|1–0]] victory for England, and one group stage game at the [[1954 FIFA World Cup]] which ended in a [[1954 FIFA World Cup Group 4#England vs Belgium|4–4]] draw.<ref name=Kit15/> Both teams had already guaranteed to advance to the last 16 before kick off, with the winner securing top spot in the group.

Both teams fielded significantly altered line-ups before the game, with media outlets stating that a loss could potentially become beneficial, as the winner would be in the half of the draw with the 4 of the top 7 sides in the world.{{efn|Belgium were ranked third, and Germany had already been eliminated. Only Switzerland (6) and Spain (10) would be on the loser's half of the draw from the top 10 of the [[FIFA World Rankings]]}}<ref>{{cite web |title=England's game v Colombia 'biggest knockout game for decade' |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44650417 |work=BBC Sport |date=28 June 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Delaney |first=Miguel |title=Three Lions still left wondering how good they really are after deflating defeat |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/world-cup-2018-england-belgium-match-report-highlights-video-batshuayi-januzaj-goal-a8422126.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220501/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/world-cup/world-cup-2018-england-belgium-match-report-highlights-video-batshuayi-januzaj-goal-a8422126.html |archive-date=1 May 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |publisher=The Independent |date=28 June 2018}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

[[Jordan Pickford]] kept out a long-range drive from [[Youri Tielemans]] before the goalkeeper was rescued by [[Gary Cahill]]'s goal-line clearance after the ball squirmed out of his grasp. In the 51st minute, [[Adnan Januzaj]] cut in from the right and hit a left foot shot into the top left corner of the net. [[Jamie Vardy]] sent [[Marcus Rashford]] through on goal in the 66th minute, but the striker's effort was turned wide of the post by a touch from [[Thibaut Courtois]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Smith |first=Jamie |title=Januzaj stunner claims Group G top spot |url=http://www.goal.com/en-om/match/england-v-belgium/2l4la1grc4tsyud191bkztecp |website=Goal.com |date=28 June 2018}}</ref>

This 1–0 victory ended Belgium's 82-year winless run against England which dates back to a friendly played in Brussels on 9 May 1936. The scoreline was 3–2 on that occasion.<ref name="ENG-BEL recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/belgium-stay-perfect-england-settle-for-second-2973464 |title=Belgium stay perfect, England finish second |publisher=FIFA |date=28 June 2018 |access-date=28 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520052930/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/belgium-stay-perfect-england-settle-for-second-2973464 |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref> This is the first World Cup match (other than 0–0 draws) in which England failed to score since a [[1986 FIFA World Cup Group F#Portugal vs England|1–0]] loss to Portugal in 1986.<ref>{{cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil |title=World Cup 2018: England lose 1-0 to Belgium in final group game |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439312 |work=BBC Sport |date=28 June 2018}}</ref>

